review_text:
enjoy story? like smashing buttons and pretty lights? like seriously how adhd are you? if you answered yes to any of these you should give sword art online fractured daydream a try. description with three epic multiplayer modes its hard to pin down think fortnite versus monsters pitting teams against on another to score higher.

you unlock modes by doing story until you get co op quests.  think of the story as the tutorial it brings you into gameplay mechanics through story. personally i love this part. as you progress through the story you unlock more characters to play. if you really need to you can skip most cutscenes. WHY other than time would you want to?  

honestley really great game not for everyone however its a great melding of game genres. waaay go peoples yall have made a great game. hands down looking forward to raise my ranks. :}

Finally a new SAO game that plays like Fatal Bullet (FB). That is, as long as you play a character that uses a gun, as his main weapon.

[b]The good[/b]:
+ Fun gameplay, with some depth to it;
+ Tons of characters to choose from and play as;
+ Long story. The devs said it takes 20 hours to complete. Took me 50+;
+ Fun coop experience;
+ Huge roster of characters to play as.

[b]The bad[/b]:
- Always online and an anticheat. I don't have a huge problem with that, but not everyone is going to like it;
- Lack of extra singleplayer content (you do get some tower thingy, once you finish the game, but I wish there was more);
- Fairly steep price atm;
- Seems kinda grindy;
- In-game monetization;
- Currently there's not many maps/bosses to fight.
- Various connectivity issues/bugs

[b]How it compares to FB[/b]:
I'd say it's an overall better game than FB. Though, currently, FB has more singleplayer content, BUT FD is still a brand new game, so you gotta cut it some slack.
